1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:05,019
Rez grid Relay listens to an audio
feed, detects configured tones, records

2
00:00:05,019 --> 00:00:09,250
dispatch audio, and creates calls for
the associated department or groups.

3
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:13,409
It can help departments connect an
existing paging process when they cannot

4
00:00:13,409 --> 00:00:15,670
modify the upstream dispatch system.

5
00:00:15,949 --> 00:00:19,300
The recording plan begins with
an approved sample audio feed

6
00:00:19,330 --> 00:00:20,959
and known tone frequencies.

7
00:00:21,369 --> 00:00:25,819
Check the input signal, configure the
intended recording behavior, and review

8
00:00:25,819 --> 00:00:27,690
the department or group recipients.

9
00:00:28,069 --> 00:00:31,600
Verify the exact installer and
interface against the supported

10
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:33,499
Relay release before capture.

11
00:00:33,629 --> 00:00:35,369
Use synthetic test audio.

12
00:00:35,840 --> 00:00:40,659
Inspect the resulting call, the captured
recording, and the intended recipients.

13
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:44,820
Test nonmatching tones separately
and document what was observed.

14
00:00:45,259 --> 00:00:49,729
The public Relay installation page
contains incomplete older steps, so it

15
00:00:49,729 --> 00:00:53,860
is a feature reference rather than a
verified modern installation procedure.

16
00:00:54,039 --> 00:00:57,980
Retain the synthetic audio
fixture, selected release, approved

17
00:00:57,980 --> 00:01:00,750
configuration, and observed test result.

18
00:01:01,219 --> 00:01:04,359
A recorder will need the
supported Relay application and

19
00:01:04,359 --> 00:01:07,920
an audio test setup to turn this
briefing into a live walkthrough.
